Per discussion need to think about this in a broader context to see if we can solve it neatly. Agree with @mchandschuh 's comment changing the CoarseFundamental Universe setting for the time in universe is OK;

Other options discussed were 
 - Changing the refresh frequency of the universe to remove these redundant securities more often than 1 day; 
 - Setting a scheduled time for the universe to run; say 8am each day, for outside of coarse time variance.
 - Setting a dynamic "minimum in universe" period for the Coarse based on when the live feed arrives.

The other current live universe timing issue is the option daily poll at midnight for the new contract list is happening when IB is closed -- resulting in any option live subscription requests failing and killing LEAN. This could also be handled with a scheduled universe event.
